\section{Concrete Physics Kernel}
The concrete N-body gravitational solver uses Plummer softening:
\[
\mathbf{F}_{12} = G \frac{m_1 m_2}{(r^2 + \epsilon^2)^{3/2}} \mathbf{r}
\]

MHD induction follows:
\[
\frac{\partial \mathbf{B}}{\partial t}
= \nabla \times (\mathbf{v} \times \mathbf{B})
\]

FHE depth increments follow:
\[
L_{t+1} = L_t + \Delta L_{\text{FHE}}
\]

with dynamic refresh when $L_{t+1} > L_{\max}$.

